        "text_preview": "And Another vs Union Of India And Others on 8 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/135507001/\n1 6."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "744c835e3cb848059daf345fb594861e_14",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In paragraph no. 4 of the order dated September 5, 2023, the Court had observed that the entire premise of the consideration of the respondent authorities was a visual inspection."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3642b8755edc4531857a70b902883302_15",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However,\nnothing is depicted in the repeated refusals by the respondent authorities, at the first instance and thereafter on the two review prayers made by the petitioners, to show as to what was the reason for accepting the pre-prints in t"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8abb0cd8893544119a4e35f36602b53e_16",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "7. In the very next paragraph, it was observed that in the absence of any such reason, the petitioners argued that the authorities ought to have physically sampled the products and satisfied themselves by appointing experts as to whether th"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "dc23d5f84c364da5a0876ba664c2217e_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. In paragraph no. 9 of the order, it was recorded that drawing of sample, it was argued, was subject to satisfactory compliance of necessary provisions of labelling and display, physical condition of the consignment/product and satisfying"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "64e567fbaf1541f2bcb06e87c5aa5037_18",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Such argument was made on behalf of the respondents."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7193134927b0489594d209f9d7162d4c_19",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. Upon fully considering the said arguments of both sides, the court came to a reasoned finding that in the present case there was nothing to indicate that there was ever any sampling or physical examination of the consignment or product t"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d9661347926e4523b272565f95517aca_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIn the absence of such examination, the refusal by the respondent authorities was held to be vitiated."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a4f0999e1db3484eaf9d88698c2cbc6f_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "10. Only in such context, in paragraph no. 18 of the judgment, the Court had directed that the respondent-authorities should also conduct a physical sample examination of the petitioners'\nproducts."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f8ab795ee6574b7290fda0e190bccd0e_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There is, in any event, no conflict between drawing of sample and physical examination of such sample."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "81fcdedc5a1c487fa87490cc231009fc_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "11. Hence, the issue now sought to be raised by the petitioner was raised at the time of deciding the writ petition and was conclusively determined."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6c6ed052e2004c08be95ece87b1bc755_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Since the order has attained finality, there is no scope of recalling the same, modifying and/or giving any clarification as the order is self-explanatory and need not be clarified further."
      },
      {
